{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/32662-pledge-help","id":32662,"title":"Pledge Help","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Changeling: The Lost"],"posts":[{"date":"2013-12-18T13:16:31-08:00","id":32662,"title":"Pledge Help","content":"So, having played in a few short-lived Changeling games off and on, when the chance for long-term Changeling game arrived I jumped at it.<br /> Then I made a Spring Courtier with the Pledge-Smithing Merit (as well as that optional merit mentioned somewhere about forcing people in to Pledges).<br /> Then I realized that I don't know much about Pledges and making them.<br /> <br /> Does anyone know which books go in to Pledges the most? I'm planning on reading through all of them. . eventually. But aside from the Core, and I imagine Rites of Spring (which I seem to recall being treated as a Second Core Book by some), are there any that go in to specific details and/or rules? I'm kinda confused on a couple of things; like what determines the relationship between the wording of the pledge and the mechanics of it. I was led to believe that the wording for Pledges is directly tied to the mechanics of it, but upon reading the sample pledges I'm seeing that isn't entirely true. Some give bonuses to skills but don't mention any of that in the Pledge itself -- especially true in the Casual version of it. Or is the wording there to protect against abuse -- if I say that the other person will get money, then that has to be in the mechanical portion, but if I simply mention that they'll get their due rewards or something, then I get to decide the actual bonus they get?<br /> <br /> And can people only get different benifits in Joint Pledges? Like I could get Resources 3 and they could get Kung Fu 3. Or does everyone get the same thing?<br /> <br /> I'm really, really hoping there's some section in some book that makes this make sense to me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/274-enokh","name":"Enokh","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar274_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"474"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-18T13:32:15-08:00","id":32679,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Enokh</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/32662-pledge-help#post32662\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> like what determines the relationship between the wording of the pledge and the mechanics of it.</div> </div> </div> </div> There's no rules linking the two, I usually choose the mechanics first then try to come up with interesting wordings afterwords. If you're trying to trick people into a Pledge you could limit the tasks to the wording you tricked people into and build the rest around that.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Enokh</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/32662-pledge-help#post32662\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> And can people only get different benifits in Joint Pledges? Like I could get Resources 3 and they could get Kung Fu 3.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-18T20:24:54-08:00","id":32927,"title":"","content":"Thanks for the reply!<br /> <br /> With the disconnect between the wording of the Pledge and the mechanics of it, is there some innate sense of what you just got in to, that way they know what actions they take (in a general sense) will break the Pledge? For instance, if someone -- stupidly -- agreed to a Pledge in which they &quot;would not rest until they found so-and-so&quot;, after the Pledge was sealed would they understand what counts as rest (sleep vs. relaxation) and what the Sanction is (Death vs. maybe a -1 Curse and a -2 Flaw)?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/274-enokh","name":"Enokh","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar274_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"474"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-18T20:26:38-08:00","id":32928,"title":"","content":"For books, you'll want to focus on the core. There's a little extra support in Rites of Spring and a section on Unwitting Pledges (when you trick someone into a Pledge they never meant to make) in Dancers in the Dusk, but the main meat of pledgecraft comes from the core. <br /> <br /> When it comes to wording vs. mechanics, the mechanics matter for things such as what you get out of it, but the wording is also very important, especially when looking for loopholes or traps in the pledge: a changeling who swore never to shed the blood of another character might still strangle or poison them safely, for example. Basically, the more vaguely the pledge is worded, the more loopholes there'll be and the more possible it will be for one or the other character to either weasel out of it or use it against another party - if they want to do so. <br /> <br /> Yes, two people can get different things out of a joint pledge. Heck, the only part of a Joint Pledge that all parties have to have in common is the Duration. Granted, most have more than that in common (be it an Alliance task, a common Endeavor or Forbiddance, or what have you), but you could easily have a motley pledge in which each person has an Alliance task in common for a month, but each also has his own individual Endeavor (one swears to build the motley's neighborhood financially, another keeps an eye out for street crime, a third keeps the motley Hollow clean and well-stocked) and gets different benefits out of it. As long as it all adds up to 0 for each party, it's all good.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1168-hobbitguy1420","name":"HobbitGuy1420","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1168_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"332"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-18T21:02:28-08:00","id":32944,"title":"","content":"Yeah, I was figuring that precise wording was more of a means to protect yourself than anything else. Oh well, might just be playing my character having the Pledge-smith Merit as a natural gift thing, and have me/him learn the little quirks as I go along.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/274-enokh","name":"Enokh","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar274_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"474"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}